  "query_preview": "..\nUpper level pattern will be progressive this week with a series\nof dry weather systems. The first dry weather system will pass\nto the north tomorrow. Cooler air will trickle down into the\nregion, setting up for below normal temperatures for Monday\nafternoon and another cold Tuesday morning. The Sulphur Springs\nValley, Upper San Pedro River Valley, and southern Greenlee \nCounty can see another round of localized freezing temperatures.\n\nDaytime temperatures will rebound to near to slightly above\nnormal Tuesday afternoon and on Wednesday under the influence \nof a ridge. The pattern will change again as another dry \nweather system passes over the region by late Wednesday to \nearly Thursday. Temperatures will be moderate for the holiday\nperiod and then trend warmer into the weekend due to a ridge\nbuilding. \n\nLooking ahead, another weather system will approach the region\nby late Sunday to early next week. Ensemble models show this \nsystem being on the wet side compared to the previous two dry \nweather systems. Yet, there are ensemble disagreement on \nplacement of trough and timing at this time. For now, 10-20% \nchances for precipitation have been introduced into the forecast\nstarting late Sunday.",
